course: dictionary
lesson: 4516
title: Headfirst
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Headfirst means with your head going in front, before the rest of your body. You can dive headfirst into a pool or slide headfirst down a slide. It can be an adverb («she dived headfirst») or an adjective («a headfirst dive»).
explain: Headfirst can also mean doing something without stopping to think, too quickly. «Don't rush headfirst into the plan» means don't jump in before you have thought it through. To tell which meaning is right, ask: is the sentence about how someone's body moves, or about how fast they act?
explain: Water safety matters here. «Empty buckets after use, because a toddler can fall headfirst into one and drown.» A toddler can fall into a bucket of water in a moment, and cannot climb out. This is why safety always comes first.
fact: Headfirst means with your head going in front of the rest of your body.
fact: Headfirst can be an adverb, as in «fell headfirst», or an adjective, as in «a headfirst dive».
fact: «Headfirst» can also mean without stopping to think first, or too quickly.
fact: Never dive headfirst into shallow or unknown water, because you can hit the bottom and break your neck.
fact: Context tells you which meaning fits: a sentence about a body position uses the first meaning, and a sentence about rushing uses the second.
exercise: «Empty buckets after use, because a toddler can fall headfirst into one and drown.» What does headfirst mean here? | Slowly and carefully | Upside down on the floor of the room | Without any water inside | *With the head going in first
exercise: Maya will rush headfirst into the new game without reading the rules. What does headfirst suggest? | *Doing it too quickly, without stopping to think | Being very careful and calm | Diving slowly into a pool | Reading every rule first
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells how he went: «He slid headfirst down the slide.» | *headfirst | slide | down | slid
test: Which is a safe rule for swimming? | Dive headfirst into any water you can see | Dive headfirst only in the sea | Dive headfirst if your friends dare you | *Never dive headfirst into shallow or unknown water
test: In «She dived headfirst into the pool», what kind of word is headfirst? | Verb | *Adverb | Pronoun | Noun
exam: Why should you always empty buckets after use? | *Because a toddler can fall headfirst into one and drown | Because the water gets cold and dirty | Because buckets are heavy to carry | Because buckets rust in the sun
